<title>INDIA: Indian Rayon 1st half '96/97 net up.</title>
<headline>Indian Rayon 1st half '96/97 net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  998.4   vs     902.5</p>
<p>    Net sales	 6,740.4   vs   5,632.7</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)    44.4   vs	40.14</p>
<p>    Other income	325.8   vs     454.6</p>
<p>    Expenditure     5,010.9   vs    4,395.1</p>
<p>    Interest	    569.4   vs	468.9</p>
<p>    Gross profit    1,485.9   vs    1,223.3</p>
<p>    Depreciation	337.5   vs	263.3</p>
<p>    Tax		   150.0   vs	 57.5</p>
<p>Note: Indian Rayon, part of the Aditya Birla group, is a leading  manufacturer of viscose filament yarn and cement. The firm said it had received dividend income of 73.8 million rupees in the first half of 1996/97 as compared to 453.3 million rupees during the year-ago period. It said it provided 36.3 million rupees out of the total dividend income for the first half of this year under the head - other income.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
